label("$\mathbf{w}$", (B + C)/2, SE);
dot("$A$", A, NW);
dot("$B$", B, SE);
dot("$C$", C, NE);
[/asy]

The area of the parallelogram determined by $\mathbf{v}$ and $\mathbf{w}$ is
\[|(-12)(-5) - (-4)(-1)| = 56,\]so the area of triangle $ABC$ is $56/2 = \boxed{28}.$

